1
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:09,800
Captain Qin.

2
00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:11,560
Coming out here like this

3
00:00:11,560 --> 00:00:13,960
means we're acting first
and reporting later.

4
00:00:14,590 --> 00:00:16,160
When Zhao finds out,

5
00:00:17,160 --> 00:00:19,190
can you say you came here alone?

6
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:20,760
When Zhao was younger

7
00:00:20,760 --> 00:00:22,000
and was
a Criminal Investigation Captain,

8
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:23,440
he used to take me along
and do the same thing.

9
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:25,800
It's fine.

10
00:00:26,030 --> 00:00:27,320
If anything happens,
I'll take responsibility.

11
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:29,710
You'll take responsibility?

12
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,960
He won't lecture you. He'll lecture me.

13
00:00:34,710 --> 00:00:36,110
What's wrong
with getting lectured a little?

14
00:00:37,030 --> 00:00:38,670
You're awfully good
at protecting yourself.

15
00:00:38,960 --> 00:00:41,000
I'm just afraid of getting scolded.

16
00:00:53,840 --> 00:00:54,520
Li.

17
00:00:54,520 --> 00:00:55,600
Go take a look over there.

18
00:01:31,150 --> 00:01:33,310
Captain Qin, I really haven't seen much.

19
00:01:34,070 --> 00:01:35,310
How come I've never heard

20
00:01:35,310 --> 00:01:36,840
of someone like this in Longfan?

21
00:01:37,870 --> 00:01:39,040
This person is incredibly rich.

22
00:01:39,040 --> 00:01:40,070
You're not the only one.

23
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:42,400
I've never
seen anything like this either.

24
00:01:43,230 --> 00:01:45,000
This is almost excessively wealthy.

25
00:01:45,310 --> 00:01:46,200
Let's go upstairs and look.

26
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:57,000
We've searched
the whole place from top to bottom,

27
00:01:57,680 --> 00:01:58,840
but there's nothing here.

28
00:01:59,510 --> 00:02:00,790
Aren't we in trouble now?

29
00:02:01,680 --> 00:02:02,790
We're done for this time.

30
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:04,510
That can't be.

31
00:02:04,950 --> 00:02:06,150
How could we be wrong?

32
00:02:10,360 --> 00:02:11,630
Qin.

33
00:02:12,360 --> 00:02:13,960
You'd better prepare to apologize.

34
00:02:24,540 --> 00:02:28,540
=Medical Examiner Dr. Qin: Bones of the Past=
=Episode 17=

35
00:02:28,740 --> 00:02:30,540
(Loyalty)

36
00:02:35,300 --> 00:02:39,380
(Longfan City PSB
Criminal Investigation Detachment)

37
00:02:40,310 --> 00:02:41,120
Stand straight!

38
00:02:41,120 --> 00:02:43,020
(Dedication, Courage,
Professionalism, Loyalty)

39
00:02:46,030 --> 00:02:47,280
You've really gotten bold.

40
00:02:47,590 --> 00:02:49,280
You're too big
for this bureau now, is that it?

41
00:02:50,080 --> 00:02:50,870
A complaint

42
00:02:51,190 --> 00:02:52,750
went straight
to the Police Inspectorate.

43
00:02:52,750 --> 00:02:53,910
I couldn't stop it even if I wanted to.

44
00:02:54,120 --> 00:02:55,870
You're a police officer, yet you entered
a private residence without permission.

45
00:02:55,870 --> 00:02:57,030
You knowingly broke the law.

46
00:02:57,120 --> 00:02:58,630
Couldn't you have told me first?

47
00:02:58,960 --> 00:03:00,960
Couldn't you wait for the search warrant
before searching the place?

48
00:03:01,310 --> 00:03:02,470
You just had
to act first and report later.

49
00:03:02,750 --> 00:03:03,520
I wasn't...

50
00:03:03,520 --> 00:03:04,910
Did I tell you to speak?

51
00:03:06,030 --> 00:03:07,280
I know what you want to say.

52
00:03:07,470 --> 00:03:08,910
You're just going to say

53
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:10,080
you were afraid
of delaying the investigation.

54
00:03:10,080 --> 00:03:10,800
Right?

55
00:03:11,120 --> 00:03:12,630
How many times have I told you?

56
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:14,150
You have to follow procedure
when investigating a case.

57
00:03:14,680 --> 00:03:16,120
You think finding the crime scene

58
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:17,400
will make up for what you did?

59
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:18,360
I just don't understand.

60
00:03:18,360 --> 00:03:19,680
That area is huge.

61
00:03:20,080 --> 00:03:21,960
Even if everyone
in the bureau helped search it,

62
00:03:21,960 --> 00:03:23,150
it would still take a day or two.

63
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:25,430
Yet you were so certain it was there.

64
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:26,910
What made you so sure?

65
00:03:27,560 --> 00:03:28,870
They're already searching the area.

66
00:03:28,910 --> 00:03:30,000
Just wait a little longer
and we'll have the results.

67
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:31,030
Are you really that impatient?

68
00:03:31,150 --> 00:03:32,470
I'm not in a hurry.

69
00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:35,400
The victims
of the Longfan fundraising case are.

70
00:03:35,470 --> 00:03:38,080
If Zhao Qian's death is connected

71
00:03:38,080 --> 00:03:39,360
to the Longfan fundraising case,

72
00:03:39,520 --> 00:03:40,310
then

73
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:42,360
we've already narrowed down
the crime scene to that area.

74
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:43,400
How did you narrow it down?

75
00:03:43,400 --> 00:03:44,590
What makes you so sure?

76
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:45,800
No, tell me.

77
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:46,910
How did you narrow it down?

78
00:03:47,870 --> 00:03:49,910
Chief, I think

79
00:03:50,150 --> 00:03:51,910
there's no need to get so worked up.

80
00:03:52,310 --> 00:03:53,840
You can just ask me calmly.

81
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:54,710
Captain Qin, come on.

82
00:03:54,710 --> 00:03:55,120
Sit.

83
00:03:55,120 --> 00:03:55,800
Sit down and tell me slowly.

84
00:03:55,800 --> 00:03:57,280
Let's hear how you narrowed it down.

85
00:03:57,280 --> 00:03:57,960
Come.

86
00:03:58,520 --> 00:03:59,310
I'd rather not sit.

87
00:03:59,470 --> 00:04:00,360
Then stand and tell me.

88
00:04:00,750 --> 00:04:02,080
You won't believe me anyway.

89
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:03,800
Just tell me. Enough nonsense.

90
00:04:05,590 --> 00:04:07,430
Don't talk to me
at one and a half speed.

91
00:04:07,430 --> 00:04:08,150
Speak properly.

92
00:04:08,150 --> 00:04:09,520
Tell me clearly, one word at a time.

93
00:04:09,840 --> 00:04:11,630
I used my walkie-talkie

94
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:14,960
to contact one of our colleagues

95
00:04:15,680 --> 00:04:17,120
30 years in the future.

96
00:04:17,630 --> 00:04:18,870
He told me

97
00:04:18,950 --> 00:04:21,630
it was in this area.

98
00:04:25,310 --> 00:04:26,270
Say that again.

99
00:04:26,390 --> 00:04:29,070
It's in this area.

100
00:04:29,390 --> 00:04:30,600
You really dare to say that.

101
00:04:32,390 --> 00:04:33,190
Do you have a fever?

102
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:35,920
Have you lost your mind?

103
00:04:37,390 --> 00:04:38,190
Qin Tian,

104
00:04:39,070 --> 00:04:40,240
you're a Criminal Investigation Captain,

105
00:04:40,480 --> 00:04:42,160
not some street
con artist making up stories.

106
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:43,680
If you don't want
to explain, then don't.

107
00:04:43,680 --> 00:04:45,190
Don't try to fool me with this nonsense.

108
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:47,950
Enough.

109
00:04:48,750 --> 00:04:50,720
You'll get a disciplinary action
and write a self-criticism.

110
00:04:51,430 --> 00:04:52,360
Then take a few days off

111
00:04:53,190 --> 00:04:54,680
and give your brain a proper rest.

112
00:04:55,190 --> 00:04:56,160
You insisted that I tell you.

113
00:04:56,270 --> 00:04:57,390
Then you don't believe me.

114
00:04:57,390 --> 00:04:58,480
Next time I'll tell you
something even crazier.

115
00:05:04,360 --> 00:05:05,160
Are you okay,

116
00:05:05,160 --> 00:05:05,950
Captain Qin.

117
00:05:06,360 --> 00:05:07,430
Did Zhao chew you out again?

118
00:05:07,430 --> 00:05:08,390
Don't stop me.

119
00:05:08,390 --> 00:05:09,630
I'm going to have a word with him today.

120
00:05:09,630 --> 00:05:10,750
I don't believe this.

121
00:05:11,870 --> 00:05:12,870
Don't stop me.

122
00:05:15,720 --> 00:05:16,720
I'm not stopping you.

123
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:18,720
Can you stop making trouble?

124
00:05:19,120 --> 00:05:21,040
I'd be grateful
if you didn't make things worse.

125
00:05:21,480 --> 00:05:23,430
Did you check the owner
of that villa as I asked?

126
00:05:23,480 --> 00:05:24,270
Yes.

127
00:05:25,310 --> 00:05:26,190
We couldn't find him.

128
00:05:26,510 --> 00:05:27,480
So I brought in

129
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:29,310
the owner's three daughters.

130
00:05:29,430 --> 00:05:30,160
Who?

131
00:05:30,160 --> 00:05:31,120
His three daughters.

132
00:05:31,190 --> 00:05:32,000
They're upstairs.

133
00:05:35,120 --> 00:05:36,040
Popcorn.

134
00:05:36,310 --> 00:05:38,360
Zheng Wei and his wife
divorced a long time ago.

135
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:39,800
She left their three daughters with him.

136
00:05:39,870 --> 00:05:42,000
Zheng Wei runs a chain of gold stores.

137
00:05:42,070 --> 00:05:44,270
I heard he went out of town
on business a couple of days ago

138
00:05:44,360 --> 00:05:45,950
and still hasn't returned.

139
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:48,920
Take a look.

140
00:05:49,070 --> 00:05:50,560
Do you recognize this man?

141
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:54,190
He doesn't look familiar.

142
00:05:54,800 --> 00:05:56,360
Never seen him. I don't know him.

143
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:57,720
I've seen him.

144
00:05:57,720 --> 00:05:59,000
That's Uncle Zhao Qian.

145
00:05:59,000 --> 00:05:59,800
Zhao Qian?

146
00:06:01,070 --> 00:06:01,870
Mr. Zheng,

147
00:06:01,920 --> 00:06:05,070
your gold store business
is doing really well.

148
00:06:05,950 --> 00:06:08,070
It's a small business.
Just enough to make a living.

149
00:06:08,070 --> 00:06:08,870
All right.

150
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:10,510
From now on, whenever any of my friends

151
00:06:10,510 --> 00:06:12,240
get married and need to buy gold,

152
00:06:12,240 --> 00:06:13,480
I'll send them all your way.

153
00:06:14,560 --> 00:06:15,390
I

154
00:06:15,390 --> 00:06:16,800
may not be good at much,

155
00:06:16,950 --> 00:06:18,190
but I do have one thing going for me.

156
00:06:18,800 --> 00:06:19,920
I have a lot of friends.

157
00:06:22,070 --> 00:06:22,870
All right, Qian.

158
00:06:23,160 --> 00:06:23,950
You're a true friend.

159
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:32,000
Thank you.

160
00:06:41,100 --> 00:06:48,300
(Longfan City PSB
Criminal Investigation Detachment)

161
00:06:48,310 --> 00:06:49,270
Well, that's a first.

162
00:06:50,160 --> 00:06:51,600
You actually remembered
to eat at mealtime.

163
00:06:52,630 --> 00:06:54,830
Your sister-in-law said eating more
flour-based foods is good for my stomach.

164
00:06:59,430 --> 00:07:02,160
Do you think Zheng Wei has already fled?

165
00:07:03,040 --> 00:07:04,070
Maybe he's on the run.

166
00:07:05,390 --> 00:07:07,040
The time and location both match.

167
00:07:11,430 --> 00:07:12,800
So why can't we find anything?

168
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:14,920
Who did this?

169
00:07:15,360 --> 00:07:16,240
Ming, right?

170
00:07:16,480 --> 00:07:17,430
A hollow wall.

171
00:07:17,920 --> 00:07:19,600
If you make the hole any bigger,
the wall will collapse.

172
00:07:20,240 --> 00:07:21,040
Ming!

173
00:07:34,040 --> 00:07:35,310
I know why now.

174
00:07:36,630 --> 00:07:37,310
Captain.

175
00:07:39,060 --> 00:07:47,580
(Police)

176
00:07:58,120 --> 00:07:59,000
What are you two doing?

177
00:07:59,000 --> 00:07:59,920
Come help.

178
00:07:59,920 --> 00:08:01,070
This thing is pretty heavy.

179
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:07,870
Only Qin Ming could come up
with an idea like this.

180
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:08,800
Exactly.

181
00:08:37,270 --> 00:08:38,360
Captain Qin,

182
00:08:38,710 --> 00:08:41,150
didn't we already come here once before?

183
00:08:41,390 --> 00:08:43,510
We searched the whole place
from top to bottom,

184
00:08:43,510 --> 00:08:44,510
but there was nothing.

185
00:08:44,790 --> 00:08:46,120
Nothing unusual.

186
00:08:52,500 --> 00:08:54,620
(Ming)

187
00:09:01,900 --> 00:09:04,740
(Ming)

188
00:09:08,390 --> 00:09:09,200
Captain Qin.

189
00:09:09,750 --> 00:09:11,030
Do you really trust

190
00:09:11,030 --> 00:09:12,910
this so-called
information from the future?

191
00:09:13,550 --> 00:09:14,670
We're police officers.

192
00:09:15,360 --> 00:09:16,600
Everything has to be based on evidence.

193
00:09:17,790 --> 00:09:19,510
According to what people say online,

194
00:09:19,550 --> 00:09:21,550
there should be gold here.

195
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:23,870
People actually
came looking for it later,

196
00:09:24,080 --> 00:09:25,910
but they didn't find anything.

197
00:09:26,630 --> 00:09:28,510
Eventually, everyone
decided it was just a rumor.

198
00:09:28,510 --> 00:09:29,630
No one came anymore.

199
00:09:29,750 --> 00:09:30,600
Captain Qin.

200
00:09:31,080 --> 00:09:33,030
Why are you going after this wall again?

201
00:09:34,390 --> 00:09:36,000
Why are you so sure

202
00:09:36,600 --> 00:09:38,600
there's a secret room in this house?

203
00:09:40,480 --> 00:09:41,600
But did you know?

204
00:09:41,910 --> 00:09:43,840
This place
was really popular for a while.

205
00:09:43,910 --> 00:09:46,240
They called it dreamcore exploration.

206
00:09:48,240 --> 00:09:50,670
We're hunting a killer across time.

207
00:09:51,960 --> 00:09:53,200
We're even using advanced technology.

208
00:09:53,200 --> 00:09:54,750
It's nothing like
their primitive methods.

209
00:09:54,750 --> 00:09:55,790
We're generations ahead.

210
00:09:57,390 --> 00:09:58,270
I believe it.

211
00:09:59,630 --> 00:10:00,910
And I'm certain

212
00:10:02,240 --> 00:10:04,030
the evidence is inside this house.

213
00:10:44,840 --> 00:10:45,670
That was too sudden.

214
00:10:45,670 --> 00:10:47,200
I wasn't ready at all.

215
00:10:57,360 --> 00:10:59,200
What are you doing? I'm down here.

216
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:00,270
Go inside and take a look.

217
00:11:02,840 --> 00:11:03,960
You're crazy.

218
00:11:27,150 --> 00:11:28,960
This is another hidden room.

219
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:30,360
You stay here.

220
00:11:30,360 --> 00:11:31,480
I don't think it's safe in there.

221
00:11:35,600 --> 00:11:36,670
You're even braver than I am.

222
00:11:56,270 --> 00:11:57,080
Lin Tao.

223
00:12:12,240 --> 00:12:13,030
Found something.

224
00:12:13,720 --> 00:12:14,480
Give it to me.

225
00:12:14,480 --> 00:12:15,200
Let me open it.

226
00:12:15,200 --> 00:12:15,870
Wait.

227
00:12:16,630 --> 00:12:17,320
What is it?

228
00:12:37,200 --> 00:12:39,720
Qin, you did it.

229
00:12:41,900 --> 00:12:42,480
(Seal)
Put it inside.

230
00:12:42,480 --> 00:12:43,720
Let's move quickly.

231
00:12:46,870 --> 00:12:47,840
Everything's here, right?

232
00:12:47,960 --> 00:12:48,960
Yes, Li. Everything's here.

233
00:12:48,960 --> 00:12:49,790
Let's go to the evidence room.

234
00:12:51,670 --> 00:12:52,440
Ming,

235
00:12:52,870 --> 00:12:54,750
we found the hidden room

236
00:12:54,750 --> 00:12:56,000
under the Little White Villa
you mentioned.

237
00:12:57,030 --> 00:12:59,120
Captain Qin, it's been
a pleasure working with you.

238
00:13:01,270 --> 00:13:03,750
The money from the Urban
Construction Group fundraising case

239
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:05,630
was converted into gold.

240
00:13:05,870 --> 00:13:07,360
Now that we've found the gold,

241
00:13:07,510 --> 00:13:09,240
they'll soon give themselves away.

242
00:13:09,360 --> 00:13:11,120
The city now plans
to gather up these gold bars,

243
00:13:11,120 --> 00:13:12,150
settle the accounts,

244
00:13:12,440 --> 00:13:14,510
and return the money to the victims
of the Urban Construction fundraising case.

245
00:13:14,840 --> 00:13:15,840
That's great.

246
00:13:15,840 --> 00:13:17,120
What about Zhao Qian's killer?

247
00:13:17,150 --> 00:13:18,080
Any leads?

248
00:13:18,150 --> 00:13:20,720
In the secret room
of the Little White Villa,

249
00:13:21,270 --> 00:13:23,000
we found a clue related to Zhao Qian.

250
00:13:24,200 --> 00:13:25,150
What clue?

251
00:13:26,240 --> 00:13:29,200
The bloodstains
on the floor matched Zhao Qian's.

252
00:13:29,200 --> 00:13:30,240
We strongly suspect

253
00:13:30,320 --> 00:13:33,030
that's where Zhao Qian died.

254
00:13:33,790 --> 00:13:34,600
We can use

255
00:13:34,630 --> 00:13:36,240
DNA testing.

256
00:13:36,480 --> 00:13:37,720
I've heard of that technology.

257
00:13:38,270 --> 00:13:39,150
How about this, Qin?

258
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:41,030
Leave the biological sample somewhere.

259
00:13:41,200 --> 00:13:42,240
As long as I can get it,

260
00:13:42,320 --> 00:13:44,150
I should be able to give you
an accurate result.

261
00:13:44,510 --> 00:13:46,080
Can you test something
from thirty years ago?

262
00:13:46,360 --> 00:13:47,480
As long as it hasn't been contaminated,

263
00:13:47,480 --> 00:13:48,320
it won't be a problem.

264
00:13:49,870 --> 00:13:51,870
That technology
isn't widely available here yet.

265
00:13:52,080 --> 00:13:52,870
Qin,

266
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:55,240
I really wish you
could come to the future

267
00:13:55,270 --> 00:13:56,670
and see this world for yourself.

268
00:13:57,480 --> 00:13:58,480
I'll try.

269
00:13:58,910 --> 00:14:00,240
Right now, I just want to know

270
00:14:00,630 --> 00:14:01,630
whether our old house is still there

271
00:14:01,630 --> 00:14:03,440
thirty years from now.

272
00:14:03,910 --> 00:14:04,720
It is.

273
00:14:05,390 --> 00:14:06,440
Mom still keeps saying

274
00:14:06,720 --> 00:14:08,320
she wants to go back
and fix up the old house.

275
00:14:08,550 --> 00:14:09,910
Don't let her
go through all that trouble.

276
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:10,790
She said

277
00:14:12,550 --> 00:14:14,910
the old house
is filled with memories of you,

278
00:14:16,120 --> 00:14:17,240
the best memories.

279
00:14:21,390 --> 00:14:22,200
Ming,

280
00:14:23,600 --> 00:14:26,550
take good care of Mom for me.

281
00:14:28,120 --> 00:14:29,240
I miss her very much.

282
00:14:30,150 --> 00:14:30,960
All right.

283
00:14:31,320 --> 00:14:33,750
Enough of this sentimental talk.

284
00:14:33,910 --> 00:14:34,840
Remember,

285
00:14:35,150 --> 00:14:36,200
I'll put the biological sample

286
00:14:36,480 --> 00:14:37,360
in the box

287
00:14:37,360 --> 00:14:39,550
where you hid your toys as a child.

288
00:14:39,790 --> 00:14:41,120
You're sure you can find it, right?

289
00:14:41,550 --> 00:14:43,480
Haven't we tested
this many times already?

290
00:14:43,910 --> 00:14:46,720
As long as it's in the same place,
I can get it.

291
00:14:48,120 --> 00:14:48,910
I'd almost forgotten.

292
00:14:55,090 --> 00:14:59,610
♪The old walkie-talkie I treasure♪

293
00:15:02,650 --> 00:15:07,450
♪The birthday surprise
you gave me that year♪

294
00:15:10,170 --> 00:15:13,950
♪Its buttons worn
and weathered with time♪

295
00:15:13,960 --> 00:15:14,750
Dad,

296
00:15:15,080 --> 00:15:17,670
your eyes are as red as a rabbit's.

297
00:15:18,150 --> 00:15:20,200
Have you ever
seen a rabbit this handsome?

298
00:15:21,270 --> 00:15:23,360
With one of us a doctor
and the other a police officer,

299
00:15:24,270 --> 00:15:26,480
we're lucky
if we even get to see each other.

300
00:15:28,080 --> 00:15:31,370
♪Rolled over our reluctance to part♪

301
00:15:32,010 --> 00:15:37,050
♪You waved goodbye
and faded into the night♪

302
00:15:39,090 --> 00:15:47,410
♪I used to think
we'd always have more time♪

303
00:15:47,410 --> 00:15:53,250
♪But that goodbye became the last♪

304
00:15:54,730 --> 00:16:02,850
♪I carry the warmth you left behind♪

305
00:16:03,530 --> 00:16:08,570
♪Making my way
through every door in life♪

306
00:16:10,370 --> 00:16:18,410
♪Whenever a train
whistle sounds at night♪

307
00:16:18,690 --> 00:16:25,930
♪I suddenly long to call out to you♪

308
00:16:26,800 --> 00:16:31,290
♪Can you hear me? Can you hear me?♪

309
00:16:31,310 --> 00:16:35,010
♪Can you hear me? Can you hear me?♪

310
00:16:35,030 --> 00:16:42,380
♪Let the old receiver
carry the words I never said♪

311
00:16:42,380 --> 00:16:48,500
♪I've taken on both
your duty and your love♪

312
00:16:48,510 --> 00:16:49,550
(Qin)

313
00:16:49,550 --> 00:16:50,840
(I think I finally understand Mom)

314
00:16:50,840 --> 00:16:52,240
(and why she's
so attached to this place.)

315
00:16:52,630 --> 00:16:53,440
(It's so warm here.)

316
00:16:54,270 --> 00:16:56,440
(Our home is so warm.)

317
00:17:01,160 --> 00:17:05,680
♪The old walkie-talkie I treasure♪

318
00:17:08,720 --> 00:17:13,520
♪The birthday surprise
you gave me that year♪

319
00:17:16,240 --> 00:17:21,600
♪Its buttons worn
and weathered with time♪

320
00:17:22,120 --> 00:17:27,480
♪Still echoing your words,
"Be brave and keep moving on"♪

321
00:17:29,480 --> 00:17:37,440
♪The old train rolled over
our reluctance to part♪

322
00:17:38,080 --> 00:17:43,120
♪You waved goodbye
and faded into the night♪

323
00:17:45,160 --> 00:17:53,480
♪I used to think
we'd always have more time♪

324
00:17:53,480 --> 00:17:59,320
♪But that goodbye became the last♪

325
00:18:00,800 --> 00:18:08,920
♪I carry the warmth you left behind♪

326
00:18:09,600 --> 00:18:14,640
♪Making my way
through every door in life♪

327
00:18:16,440 --> 00:18:24,480
♪Whenever a train
whistle sounds at night♪

328
00:18:24,760 --> 00:18:32,000
♪I suddenly long to call out to you♪

329
00:18:32,200 --> 00:18:36,640
♪Can you hear me?♪

330
00:18:36,640 --> 00:18:40,440
♪Can you hear me?♪

331
00:18:40,440 --> 00:18:47,880
♪Let the old receiver
carry the words I never said♪

332
00:18:47,880 --> 00:18:55,640
♪I've taken on
both your duty and your love♪

333
00:18:55,960 --> 00:19:01,560
♪This train has no return, and when I
look back, you're no longer waiting♪

334
00:19:03,440 --> 00:19:07,040
♪After all these years♪

335
00:19:09,560 --> 00:19:17,040
♪How I wish I could
talk to you just one more time♪

336
00:19:17,920 --> 00:19:19,240
♪And tell you♪

337
00:19:20,440 --> 00:19:23,720
♪I haven't let you down♪
